Deploy Apache HTTP Server via Docker Compose on App Server 3
This project sets up a containerized Apache HTTP Server (httpd) using Docker Compose on Application Server 3 (stapp03) to host static website content provided by the Nautilus application development team.

Requirements
Target Server: App Server 3 (stapp03)

Docker Compose File: /opt/docker/docker-compose.yml

Container Name: httpd

Image: httpd:latest

Port Mapping: Host port 5001 mapped to container port 80

Volume Mapping: Host directory /opt/devops mounted to container path /usr/local/apache2/htdocs

Configuration File (/opt/docker/docker-compose.yml)
YAML
services:
  web:
    image: httpd:latest
    container_name: httpd
    ports:
      - "5001:80"
    volumes:
      - /opt/devops:/usr/local/apache2/htdocs
    restart: always
Deployment Steps
Connect to App Server 3:

Bash
ssh banner@stapp03
(Password: BigGr33n)

Create the Docker Directory:

Bash
sudo mkdir -p /opt/docker
Create and Populate the Compose File:
Write the configuration above into /opt/docker/docker-compose.yml.

Start the Container:

Bash
cd /opt/docker
sudo docker compose up -d
Verify the Deployment:

Bash
sudo docker ps
